Taken from the published crate, not a git checkout. The checksum above is the
crates.io checksum of xdvdfs-0.8.3.crate and was verified against the registry.

`also-reflects` matters because it is not a feature toggle. In 0.8.3 `mod remap;`
and `pub use remap::*;` in write/fs/mod.rs are UNCONDITIONAL - there is no way to
build `write` without `wax`. Upstream 6b05af7 (merged 2026-07-18) is what makes
remap optional, and this tree reaches the same end state by deleting the module
outright. So the content here is 0.8.3 plus the outcome of that commit with
remap off, not plain 0.8.3.

crates.io is still on 0.8.3 as of 2026-07-25 and its `write` feature still lists
`wax`, so the de-vendoring described in docs/vendor-code.md remains blocked on
upstream cutting a release that contains 6b05af7. Re-check with:
`curl -s https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/xdvdfs | jq '.versions[0] | {num, features}'`

The inlined tree is not byte-identical to the release. Audited against 0.8.3 on
2026-07-25 by copying both trees to a neutral directory, rewriting
`crate::xdvdfs::` back to `crate::`, and diffing: 14 of 16 files pair up and
differ by 238 lines. Unlike nod, formatting is NOT a factor here - neither
upstream nor this repo has a rustfmt.toml, so both use stable defaults. Every
difference falls into one of these, and there are NO functional divergences:

  features    The pinned set (std, read, write, sync on; logging, checksum,
              ciso_support off) is resolved rather than gated, so
              `#[cfg(feature = ...)]` lines are deleted and disabled code with
              them. This is most of the diff. checksum.rs goes with its feature.
              The traceln!/debugln! macros are stubbed to expand to nothing
              because `logging` is off.
  remap       write/fs/remap.rs and its `mod`/`pub use` lines are gone. NOT a
              feature toggle in 0.8.3 - see `also-reflects` above.
  no_std      `#![no_std]` and the `extern crate` lines are dropped; crate-level
              attributes cannot apply to a module. `extern crate alloc;` lives in
              the rom-weaver-containers root instead.
  docs        mod.rs carries a ~28 line inlining header that upstream has no
              equivalent of.
  edition     This workspace is edition 2024 and a newer clippy, so: let chains
              (write/avl.rs), `ref` bindings dropped for match ergonomics
              (util.rs), `% n > 0` -> `!is_multiple_of(n)` (layout.rs,
              write/dirtab.rs), and `<'_>` lifetime elision in several signatures.
              Upstream 0.8.3 does not parse under edition 2024, so a diff has to
              format each side under its own edition.
  deps        layout.rs drops `#[repr(C)]` on a bitfield newtype - proc-bitfield
              0.5 makes those `#[repr(transparent)]` itself and the explicit
              attribute became a hard error. Layout is unchanged.
  tests       layout.rs's 2 test fns are dropped because they need
              `futures::executor` and `futures` is not a dependency of
              rom-weaver-containers. util.rs (3) and write/avl.rs (6) keep theirs.
              This is the one difference that costs coverage; restore it by
              adding `futures` as a dev-dependency if the tests are wanted.

So: diff against the release expecting differences, and re-sync deliberately. If
a diff ever shows something outside these categories, it is a real divergence.
